### Interview-Ready Answer

A good Socket.IO React integration normally uses a shared socket instance, manages connection lifetime at an application-level boundary, and subscribes to feature events inside Effects with matching cleanup. Event listeners should not be repeatedly registered on every reconnection or render. Authentication should be verified by the server, while React components consume socket events and update their own feature state.
